{
  "_about": "IGF M04 s10 'A leak - up or down? Predict, then watch' - the hand-made m04_leak3d.js (1,565 lines) as a 3D-kit spec. A 6 x 3 x 4 m machinery space, open at the front (z = +2); floor top y = 0, deckhead y = 3, x to the right, 1 unit = 1 m. The gas pipe (DN150) enters the left wall at 1.5 m, runs through a valve to a flange that leaks and rises to the deckhead; the leak is the origin of every gas part. One gas part per fuel (six buttons = six controls, one fuel at a time); the propane and cold-methane clouds have a second small part that falls into the bilge well. Dropped from the original: the caption chip (the fuel's name and what it does is a label here), the cold methane warming and lifting after 5 s (kit: no 'then'), the oily water in the well, floor and wall seams. The bilge well is boxes under the room's thin floor, seen under its front edge.",
  "label": "3D model of a closed machinery space cut open: the deckhead with its beams, the floor plates, a bilge well sunk below the floor, a pump set, an electrical cabinet, a ladder, and a gas pipe with an isolating valve and a flange at mid height that leaks. One button for each of six fuels plays its vapour cloud: warm natural gas, ammonia and hydrogen rise to the deckhead, propane and cold methane sink to the floor and the bilge, methanol stays and mixes near the leak.",
  "units": "m",
  "view": {"az": 31.5, "el": 17.2, "fill": 1.0},
  "controls_at": "right",
  "captions": [
    {"text": "Cold methane: sinks and spreads low - warms above about -110 °C, then it rises", "when": "g_cold.on > 0.5"},
    {"text": "Warm natural gas: rises to the deckhead", "when": "g_warm.on > 0.5"},
    {"text": "Propane: sinks to the lowest place and stays there", "when": "g_propane.on > 0.5"},
    {"text": "Methanol vapour: stays near the spill and mixes with the air", "when": "g_methanol.on > 0.5"},
    {"text": "Ammonia: lighter than air - it rises", "when": "g_ammonia.on > 0.5"},
    {"text": "Hydrogen: rises fastest of all", "when": "g_hydrogen.on > 0.5"}
  ],
